{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When a soul sins unwittingly.</b> The word <b>נפש</b> ('soul') is the joining of the soul with the body together, for you find in the account of Creation that it is written (Genesis 2:7): ״וייצר ה' אלהים את האדם עפר מן האדמה״ — 'And YHWH Elohim formed the man, dust from the earth'; and when the two of them, body and soul, were joined, He called them נפש, as it says (ibid.): ״ויהי האדם לנפש חיה״ — 'and the man became a living soul.' For the word אדם ('man') is the conjunction of body and soul, and likewise the word הנפש ('the soul') means the conjunction of body and soul, because merit and sin belong to both of them together, and each one alone has no capacity either to merit or to be punished. And this is what is written (Leviticus 17:10): ״ונתתי פני בנפש האוכלת את הדם״ — 'and I will set My face against the soul that eats the blood'; yet we see that it is the body that eats and drinks and performs all the functions of the other senses, and it says בנפש האוכלת — 'the soul that eats.' This is proof that Scripture calls the conjunction of body and soul נפש. And this is why Scripture concludes: ״והכרתי אותו מקרב עמו״ — 'and I will cut him off from among his people' — after it mentioned the feminine form, it reverted to the body in the masculine form. And so it says here: נפש כי תחטא בשגגה — 'when a soul sins unwittingly' — and then it says ועשה, which is masculine. And immediately it mentions: 'if the anointed priest sins,' for he is composed of soul and body. And since we find in the account of Creation that it mentioned the joining of body and soul in the language of נפש, therefore it used the word נפש in some of the commandments, and the intention is not the soul without the body, but rather the body of man together with his soul. And sometimes you find in Scripture the word אדם, and the meaning is the soul together with the body. However, we sometimes find the body alone referred to in the language of נפש, as it is written (I Kings 20:31): ״אולי יחיה את נפשך״ — 'perhaps he will let your soul live'; and likewise (Numbers 23:10): ״תמות נפשי מות ישרים״ — 'let my soul die the death of the upright' — yet there is no death for the soul. And the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: <b>נפש כי תחטא</b> — to include converts and slaves." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'When a soul sins unwittingly' — this is what Scripture says (Proverbs 19:2): ״גם בלא דעת נפש לא טוב ואץ ברגלים חוטא״ — 'Also without knowledge the soul is not good, and he who hastens with his feet sins.' This refers to Ahab son of Kolaiah and Zedekiah son of Maaseiah, who used to sin in Jerusalem, and it was not enough, but when they were exiled to Babylon they continued to add sin. And what were they doing in Jerusalem? They were false prophets, and they abandoned their trade in Babylon and would pimp for each other in matters of forbidden relations. Ahab son of Kolaiah would enter the homes of the great ones of the kingdom and say: 'I am so-and-so, a prophet; the Holy One, blessed be He, sent me to say something to your wife.' And the man would say to him: 'Here she is before you.' He would go in and be intimate with her and say to her: 'The Holy One, blessed be He, seeks to raise up prophets from you — go and lie with Zedekiah son of Maaseiah and you will bear prophets from him.' And she would listen to him and send for Zedekiah, and he would come and lie with her. And likewise Zedekiah would pimp for Ahab in the same manner, and this was their trade. Come and see how wicked they were: they made a name for themselves in Babylon as great prophets. If a woman was pregnant, they would tell her that she would give birth to a male, and they would tell her neighbors that she would give birth to a female. If she gave birth to a male, she would say: 'The words of the prophet were fulfilled.' And if she gave birth to a female, her neighbors would say to her: 'Thus the prophet told us, but he did not wish to distress you.' And they continued doing this until they reached the wife of Nebuchadnezzar. Zedekiah said to her: 'The Holy One, blessed be He, sent me to you — go and lie with Ahab and you will bear prophets from him.' She said to him: 'I will not do this except with the king's knowledge.' She reported the matter to the king. King Nebuchadnezzar sent for them and said to them: 'Is this what you said to my wife?' They said to him: 'The Holy One, blessed be He, wishes to raise up prophets from her.' The king said to them: 'I have heard from your Elohim that He hates licentiousness — Zimri son of Salu, because he broke forth in whoredom, caused twenty-four thousand to fall from Israel, and you say such things! Whether you are true prophets or false prophets, I do not know. But I tested Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah and I heated the furnace for seven days, and they emerged whole. For you I will not heat it for more than one day — if you are saved, I will know for certain that you are true prophets, and I will agree to everything you say.' They said to him: 'Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah were three, and the miracle was performed by means of three, but we are only two.' He said to them: 'There is a third here like you.' They said to him: 'There is Joshua son of Jehozadak the High Priest.' They thought they would be saved by his merit. They threw him into the furnace with them — the two of them were burned, and he was saved, as it is written (Zechariah 3:2): ״הלא זה אוד מוצל מאש״ — 'Is not this a brand plucked from the fire?' And from Ahab and Zedekiah (Jeremiah 29:22) a curse was taken up among all the exile of Judah that is in Babylon, saying: 'May Elohim make you like Zedekiah and like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire.' What caused these wicked men to be burned? That they were ״אץ ברגלים״ — 'hasty with their feet' — after transgressions. Therefore it says: ואץ ברגלים חוטא."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:59.567390447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}